Package: bear
Version: VERSION_PLACEHOLDER
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: ARCH_PLACEHOLDER
Maintainer: Bear Development Team <bear@example.com>
Description: Tool that generates a compilation database for clang tooling
 Bear is a tool that generates a compilation database for clang tooling.
 It intercepts compiler calls during the build process and records them
 in a JSON format that can be used by clang-based tools like clang-tidy,
 clangd, and other static analysis tools.
 .
 The package installs the layout described in Bear/INSTALL.md.
 bear-driver is compiled with `INTERCEPT_LIBDIR=$LIB`; glibc's ld.so
 expands `$LIB` to the Debian multiarch subpath per process
 architecture (e.g. `lib/x86_64-linux-gnu` for 64-bit,
 `lib/i386-linux-gnu` for 32-bit), so the correct libexec.so is
 loaded automatically:
  - /usr/bin/bear                                       (shell script -> bear-driver)
  - /usr/libexec/bear/bin/bear-driver
  - /usr/libexec/bear/bin/bear-wrapper
  - /usr/libexec/bear/MULTIARCH_LIBDIR_PLACEHOLDER/libexec.so
Homepage: https://github.com/rizsotto/Bear
